          "via": "plan",
          "ticket": null,
          "requirements": [
            {
              "name": "build-go-command",
              "text": "Implement in Go 1.22 or newer using only the standard library. The application root is a Go module, and its executable is the main package at `./cmd/dupfind`.",
              "stories": []
            },
            {
              "name": "command-options-and-validation",
              "text": "dupfind [--summary] [--min-size <bytes>] <directory>",
              "stories": [
                "command_interface"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "walk-and-filter-files",
              "text": "1. **Scope.** The tool walks `<directory>` recursively, including hidden files and directories\n(names beginning `.`). It considers regular files only. It neither follows nor reports\nsymbolic links.\n2. **Empty files are never duplicates.** A file of zero bytes is always ignored, which the\ndefault `--min-size 1` guarantees.\n3. **Duplicate test.** Files are grouped by size first. Only files that share a size are read.\nWithin a size, files are grouped by the SHA-256 digest of their contents. A group of two or\nmore files with the same size and digest is a duplicate group.",
              "stories": [
                "duplicate_discovery"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "listing-csv-output",
              "text": "**Listing** (default): header `group,size,sha256,path`, then one row per file in every duplicate\ngroup. `sha256` is the lowercase hexadecimal digest. With no duplicates, only the header is\nwritten.",
              "stories": [
                "listing_output"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ordered-groups-and-paths",
              "text": "5. **Order.** Groups are ordered by reclaimable bytes descending, then by digest ascending.\nA group's reclaimable bytes are `size \u00d7 (files \u2212 1)`. Groups are numbered from 1 in that order.\nWithin a group, paths are ordered by byte value ascending.",
              "stories": [
                "listing_output"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "summary-csv-output",
              "text": "**Summary** (`--summary`): header `groups,duplicate_files,reclaimable_bytes`, then one row.\n`duplicate_files` is the sum of `files \u2212 1` over all groups. `reclaimable_bytes` is the sum of\nevery group's reclaimable bytes. With no duplicates the row is `0,0,0`.",
              "stories": [
                "summary_output"
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "verification-suite",
              "text": "The completed application provides a POSIX-compatible `bin/test.sh` that runs `go vet ./...` and `go test ./...` from the application root and exits zero only when both pass. The suite covers\neach rule, each output form, and each exit code against real temporary directories.",
              "stories": [
                "verification"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
